1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-5","kind":"phase-index","route":"/roadmap/phase-5","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-5","sourceHash":"4549bde84d59d4e7c4061fd2a658ac1c4790464ce7efc5b9fd9514271f4e3c23","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:56.712Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Accuracy","zh":"准确性"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You can speak, you can understand, and you can get by in the language. But you know your output is rough around the edges — you with grammar commit mistakes, use phrasing on an awkward sort, and sometimes reach for the wrong wart. Phase 5 is about cleaning that up.","zh":"你已经能够说这门语言，能够理解，也能用它应付日常交流。但你知道自己的输出还有不少瑕疵——语法会犯错，措辞有时别扭，偶尔还会用错词。第5阶段就是要把这些问题整理好。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The tool for this job is writing. It might seem counterintuitive to focus on writing when you want to improve your speaking, but writing gives you something speaking doesn't: time.","zh":"完成这项工作的工具是写作。想提高口语，却把重点放在写作上，似乎有些反直觉；但写作能提供口语无法提供的东西：时间。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"When you write, you can pause, think, look things up, revise, and analyze your own mistakes. You build accuracy slowly and deliberately on paper, then transfer it to speech.","zh":"写作时，你可以暂停、思考、查找资料、修改，并分析自己的错误。你先在纸面上缓慢而有意识地建立准确性，再将其迁移到口语中。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This is also the phase where formal grammar study becomes truly valuable. In earlier phases, grammar study was supplementary — a way to prime yourself for patterns you'd encounter in immersion. Now, you're using grammar to refine and correct your output. You already have strong intuitions about the language; grammar study helps you identify exactly where those intuitions are wrong and fix them.","zh":"正式的语法学习也在这一阶段真正变得有价值。在早期阶段，语法学习只是辅助工具——帮助你为沉浸中会遇到的模式做好预热。现在，你要利用语法来完善并纠正自己的输出。你已经对这门语言形成了很强的直觉；语法学习能帮助你准确找出这些直觉出错的地方，并加以修正。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By the end of Phase 5, you'll be comfortable speaking and writing at roughly the level of a high school student in the language — around B2. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/cefr-levels\">CEFR Levels</a>","zh":"到第5阶段结束时，你会能够较为自如地进行口语和写作，水平大致相当于该语言环境中的高中生——约为B2。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/cefr-levels\">CEFR等级</a>"}},{"id":"hour-estimates","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Hour Estimates","zh":"时间估算"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"","zh":"","header":true},{"en":"Cousin","zh":"近亲语言","header":true},{"en":"Similar","zh":"相近语言","header":true},{"en":"Neutral","zh":"中等距离","header":true},{"en":"Distant","zh":"远亲语言","header":true}],[{"en":"This phase","zh":"本阶段","header":false},{"en":"135","zh":"135","header":false},{"en":"225","zh":"225","header":false},{"en":"300","zh":"300","header":false},{"en":"450","zh":"450","header":false}],[{"en":"Cumulative","zh":"累计","header":false},{"en":"665","zh":"665","header":false},{"en":"1150","zh":"1150","header":false},{"en":"1400","zh":"1400","header":false},{"en":"2250","zh":"2250","header":false}]]},{"id":"sub-phases","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Sub-phases","zh":"子阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>5A — Writing Comfort:</strong> Get comfortable with the mechanics of writing — typing, keyboard layout, putting your thoughts on paper.","zh":"<strong>5A——写作舒适度：</strong>熟悉写作的基本操作——打字、键盘布局，以及把想法写下来。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>5B — Writing Accuracy:</strong> Use writing to identify and fix your most common errors in grammar, word choice, and expression.","zh":"<strong>5B——写作准确性：</strong>通过写作找出并纠正你在语法、选词和表达方面最常见的错误。"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>5C — Speaking Accuracy:</strong> Transfer what you've learned through writing into your spoken language.","zh":"<strong>5C——口语准确性：</strong>将你通过写作学到的内容迁移到口语表达中。"}},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The decision to focus on writing as the primary tool for developing accuracy reflects research on the cognitive advantages of writing in language learning. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jslw.2012.09.006\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Williams (2012)</a> identified three features of writing that make it particularly effective for language development: its slower pace allows for more cognitive processing, the permanent record it leaves enables review and revision, and the need for precision encourages learners to consult their explicit knowledge while planning and monitoring their output. These are processes that are largely impossible under the time pressure of real-time conversation.","zh":"选择将写作作为培养准确性的主要工具，反映了语言学习研究中关于写作认知优势的发现。<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jslw.2012.09.006\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Williams（2012）</a>指出，写作有三个特点，使其特别适合语言发展：较慢的节奏允许进行更多认知加工；留下的永久记录便于复习和修改；对精确性的要求促使学习者在规划和监控输出时调动显性知识。这些过程在实时对话的时间压力下基本无法完成。"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The Phase 4 → Phase 5 progression is supported by research on fossilization and interlanguage. <a href=\"https://www.multilingual-matters.com/page/detail/Fossilization-in-Adult-Second-Language-Acquisition/?k=9781853596865\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Han (2004)</a> documented how errors that persist uncorrected can become resistant to change. However, attempting accuracy before basic fluency is established is counterproductive — learners need sufficient volume and practice to develop robust interlanguage systems before targeted error correction becomes effective. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1515/iral.1972.10.1-4.209\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Selinker (1972)</a> established that learners operate within an evolving interlanguage system shaped by both input exposure and output practice. Phase 5's structure — comfort with production first, then deliberate accuracy work — ensures that learners have a stable enough system to benefit from correction.","zh":"第 4 阶段 → 第 5 阶段的进阶得到了关于僵化和中介语的研究支持。<a href=\"https://www.multilingual-matters.com/page/detail/Fossilization-in-Adult-Second-Language-Acquisition/?k=9781853596865\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Han（2004）</a>记录了未经纠正而持续存在的错误如何变得难以改变。然而，在基本流利度形成之前就追求准确性会适得其反——学习者需要足够的输入量和练习，先建立稳固的中介语系统，然后有针对性的错误纠正才会真正有效。<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1515/iral.1972.10.1-4.209\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Selinker（1972）</a>指出，学习者运作于一个不断发展的中介语系统中，这一系统同时受到输入接触和输出练习的影响。第 5 阶段先培养舒适的表达能力，再进行有意识的准确性训练，确保学习者拥有足够稳定的语言系统，从纠正中获益。"}}],"cards":[{"href":"/roadmap/phase-5/5a-writing-comfort","title":{"en":"5AWriting Comfort","zh":"5A写作舒适度"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-5/5b-writing-accuracy","title":{"en":"5BWriting Accuracy","zh":"5B写作准确性"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-5/5c-speaking-accuracy","title":{"en":"5CSpeaking Accuracy","zh":"5C口语准确性"}}]}}]
